    "q-269923": {
      "dom_id": "step-q269923",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "If $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are polynomials of degree $12$,  the highest possible degree of $P+Q$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The highest possible degree of $P+Q$ is $12.$\n\nFor example, suppose $P={x}^{12}$ and $Q={x}^{12}.$ Then $P+Q=2{x}^{12}.$ \n\nSince neither $P$ nor $Q$ contain terms of order higher than ${x}^{12},$ $P+Q$ can't contain terms of order higher than ${x}^{12}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
