    "q-277912": {
      "dom_id": "step-q277912",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "If $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are polynomials of degree $7$, the **smallest possible** degree of $P+Q$ is{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The smallest possible degree of $P-Q$ is $0.$\n\nFor example, suppose $P=9{x}^{7}$ and $Q=-9{x}^{7}-4.$ Then $P+Q=-4,$ which is a polynomial of degree $0.$",
